{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "def triples_sum_to_zero(l: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    triples_sum_to_zero takes a list of integers as an input.\n    it returns True if there are three distinct elements in the list that\n    sum to zero, and False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(l)\n    if n < 3:\n        return False\n\n    # Store (value, original_index) pairs to maintain distinctness by index\n    indexed_nums = []\n    for i, num in enumerate(l):\n        indexed_nums.append((num, i))\n\n    # Sort the list based on values\n    indexed_nums.sort()\n\n    for i in range(n - 2):\n        # Fix one element, indexed_nums[i]\n        # Use two pointers for the rest of the array\n        left = i + 1\n        right = n - 1\n\n        while left < right:\n            val_i = indexed_nums[i][0]\n            val_left = indexed_nums[left][0]\n            val_right = indexed_nums[right][0]\n\n            current_sum = val_i + val_left + val_right\n\n            if current_sum == 0:\n                return True\n            elif current_sum < 0:\n                left += 1\n            else:\n                right -= 1\n    return False"}
