{"task_id": "HumanEval/163", "solution": "def generate_integers(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given two positive integers a and b, return the even digits between a\n    and b, in ascending order.\n\n    For example:\n    generate_integers(2, 8) => [2, 4, 6, 8]\n    generate_integers(8, 2) => [2, 4, 6, 8]\n    generate_integers(10, 14) => []\n    \"\"\"\n    even_digits = [2, 4, 6, 8]\n    \n    # Normalize the range to ensure min_val is always less than or equal to max_val.\n    min_val = min(a, b)\n    max_val = max(a, b)\n    \n    result = []\n    for digit in even_digits:\n        # Check if the even digit is within the normalized inclusive range.\n        if min_val <= digit <= max_val:\n            result.append(digit)\n            \n    return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/163", "solution": "def generate_integers(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given two positive integers a and b, return the even digits between a\n    and b, in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    EVEN_DIGITS = [0, 2, 4, 6, 8]\n\n    min_val = min(a, b)\n    max_val = max(a, b)\n\n    result = []\n    for digit in EVEN_DIGITS:\n        if min_val <= digit <= max_val:\n            result.append(digit)\n    return result"}
